# Delvers D-048 presentation audit

Live, bounded follow-up to [Phase 6](DELVERS_CAMPAIGN_CLEANUP_PLAN.md#5a-d-048-reader-first-consolidation--focused-follow-up-2026-10-28). This supplements the dated baseline; it does not replace earlier factual or editorial acceptance. Authorization: D-048 presentation approval and the owner's instruction to read the updated plan and proceed, 2026-10-28. D-047 remains standing permission for minor copyedits.

## Batch 01 — campaign, narrative and world portals

| Page | Purpose and source horizon | D-048 reader-first disposition | Finding and treatment |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| [Campaign portal](../delvers/README.md) | Entry to three completed arcs; through S3E12 and the one-year epilogue | compliant | Story opening, reading routes and lore precede a closing Sources and project notes section. Recently owner-reworked page retained byte-for-byte. |
| [Narrative portal](../delvers/narrative/README.md) | Primary reading order and four earlier detailed studies; through S3E12, with each study's own earlier coverage | compliant after presentation pass | Archive IDs, Academy source placement and historical-version/link-compatibility explanation moved below reading routes into Sources and project notes. Opening and study introduction now describe the story. |
| [World portal](../delvers/world/README.md) | World directory; campaign coverage through S3E12, each subject limited to its last supported observation | compliant | World opening and subject directory precede closing project notes. Cleanup progress, research boundaries and compatibility records already sit there. Retained byte-for-byte. |

Expected and resulting order: story/world introduction → reading or subject routes → historical detailed-reading routes where applicable → Sources and project notes. No paths, titles, link destinations, existing headings, footnotes, images or approved arc boundaries change. Academy placement remains qualified by the existing narrative guidance; no new chronology finding is made. The final invitation and unopened letter retain their evidence limits. Listening remains deferred by owner.

Exact working-copy originals, hashes and rebased reading copies are in the [batch archive](../research/legacy/2026-10-28/delvers-d048-portals-01/README.md). The [report](../reports/DELVERS_D048_PORTALS_01_2026-10-28.md) and [validation record](DELVERS_D048_PORTALS_01_2026-10-28.json) record bounded acceptance and its limits.

## Batch 02 — Characters and Places

| Page | Purpose and source horizon | D-048 reader-first disposition | Finding and treatment |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| [Characters](../delvers/world/CHARACTERS.md) | People and reasoning communities; latest supported observations through S3E12, with separately attributed post-finale character-design commentary | compliant after presentation pass | Role/history column replaces performer/source labels. Cast credits, episode identifiers, clocks, phonetic/orthography warnings and legacy-slug detail move to cited closing notes. Names, row order, profile routes, testimony and unresolved outcomes remain. |
| [Places](../delvers/world/PLACES.md) | Locations and institutions; latest supported observations through S3E12 and the one-year epilogue | compliant after presentation pass | Nature/history column and city description lead with the world. Map/ASR procedure, recording locators, source placement and evidence links move to cited closing notes. Map forms and ASR aliases retain distinct authority; the farm/cave association stays contextual. |

The complete two-index source was reviewed before and after editing. Expected and resulting order: world introduction → subject tables and connections → Sources and project notes, including referenced note definitions. All pre-existing Markdown destinations, their multiplicities, existing headings and table row order are retained. The new footnotes relocate apparatus; they do not close identity, source-clock or listening questions. No permanent membership, child abduction, living Radiant Lance, performed final wedding, opened letter, final rescue count or unshown restoration is inferred.

[Report](../reports/DELVERS_D048_INDEXES_02_2026-10-28.md) · [Validation](DELVERS_D048_INDEXES_02_2026-10-28.json) · [Exact originals, hashes, rebased reading copies and guarded edits](../research/legacy/2026-10-28/delvers-d048-indexes-02/README.md). Five priority-one pages now have recorded dispositions; the remaining priority-one pages and subject samples are still open.

## Remaining scope and next batch

Next: review [Creatures and monsters](../delvers/world/CREATURES_AND_MONSTERS.md) and the [setting study](../delvers/world/WORLD.md), check for any other published reader indexes, then inspect a bounded sample of biographies, institutions, places, artifacts and creatures. Expand subject checks only for demonstrated defects. Unreviewed pages are not certified compliant by earlier cleanup or by these two batches.

Source inventory, episode dossiers, source-keyed chronology, consistency ledger and technical/review registers are retained evidence-first exceptions under the plan; their functional classification is not a new content audit. Primary narrative bodies and earlier detailed studies are not rewritten by this batch. No issue is closed and no claim of whole-campaign D-048 completion is made.
